namespace Work.MotC2

/-
NOTE: an earlier refutation of this statement was for a stale definition.  `infIdeal` is now a
`Submodule (infCoordRing E) (Func E)` (the maximal ideal of the CHART RING `infCoordRing E`, not an
ideal of the field `Func E`), and `infPlace E` is now the localization of `infCoordRing E` at that
maximal ideal, i.e. the ring of functions regular at `O`.  Please re-read
`Submission/Work/MotC2/Defs.lean` (definitions `infCoordRing`, `infIdeal`, `infPlace`) before
proving this.

Proof route.  (1) `infPlace E` contains `infCoordRing E` and the inverse of every element of
`infCoordRing E` outside `infIdeal E`; its non-units are exactly the elements of the ideal
`infIdeal E · infPlace E`.  (2) `u = 1/x` and `w = y/x²` satisfy
`w² + a₁uw + a₃u²w = u + a₂u² + a₄u³ + a₆u⁴` (`Relations`), so `u·h = w²` with
`h = 1 + a₂u + a₄u² + a₆u³ - a₁w - a₃uw` a unit of the localization; hence the maximal ideal is
principal, generated by `infW E`.  (3) `Func E` is the fraction field of `infPlace E` (it contains
`u, w`, hence `x = u⁻¹` and `y = w u⁻²`), the ring is Noetherian and not a field, so
`IsDiscreteValuationRing` follows from `IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE` (item 4, principal maximal
ideal).  (4) The residue field is `L` since `w = 0` and `u = 0` in `infPlace E ⧸ (infW E)`.  Beware
that `IsRatPlace` also requires that `Func E` is generated over `L` as the fraction field of the
subalgebra (second conjunct of `IsRatPlace`): use `x = u⁻¹`, `y = w u⁻²`.

The proof is split as follows.

* `Work.MotC2.InfPlaceSetup` (module `Submission.Work.MotC2.InfPlaceSetup`): the ideal
  `infIdealR E = ⟨u, w⟩` of the chart ring `infCoordRing E`; the proof that it is *proper*
  (`one_notMem_infIdealR`, a degree argument using `x ^ (m+4)` and the `L[X]`-basis `{1, y}` of
  `L[x,y]`), that it is maximal (`isMaximal_infIdealR`, via `infCoordRing E ⊆ L + ⟨u,w⟩`), the
  membership description `infPlace_mem_iff` of `infPlace E` as fractions, and the fact that
  `↥(infPlace E)` is the localization of `infCoordRing E` at `⟨u,w⟩`
  (`instIsLocalizationInfPlace`), hence local and Noetherian.
* `Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore` (module `Submission.Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore`): the relation
  `u·h = w·α` with `h = 1 + a₂u + a₄u² + a₆u³` and `α = w + a₁u + a₃u²`, giving
  `maxIdeal_eq_span`: the maximal ideal of `↥(infPlace E)` is generated by the image of `w`; the
  discrete valuation ring instance `instIsDiscreteValuationRing` (via
  `IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE`); `residue_field`: the residue field is `L`; `frac_field`: `L(E)`
  is the fraction field of `infPlace E`; and the dichotomy `infW_mul_of_not_unit` /
  `infW_not_unit`.
-/
theorem InfPlace (L : Type*) [Field L] (E : WeierstrassCurve L) [E.IsElliptic] :
    Work.MotC2.IsRatPlace E (Work.MotC2.infPlace E) ∧
    Work.MotC2.infW E ∈ Work.MotC2.infPlace E ∧
    (¬ ∃ g ∈ Work.MotC2.infPlace E, Work.MotC2.infW E * g = 1) ∧
    (∀ f : Work.MotC2.Func E, f ∈ Work.MotC2.infPlace E →
      (¬ ∃ g ∈ Work.MotC2.infPlace E, f * g = 1) →
      ∃ g : Work.MotC2.Func E, g ∈ Work.MotC2.infPlace E ∧ f = Work.MotC2.infW E * g) := by
  have hdvr : IsDiscreteValuationRing ↥(infPlace E) := InfPlaceCore.instIsDiscreteValuationRing E
  have hrat : IsRatPlace E (infPlace E) :=
    ⟨Exists.intro hdvr (InfPlaceCore.residue_field E), InfPlaceCore.frac_field E⟩
  exact ⟨hrat, InfPlaceCore.infW_mem_infPlace E, InfPlaceCore.infW_not_unit E,
    fun f hf h => InfPlaceCore.infW_mul_of_not_unit E f hf h⟩

end Work.MotC2
